+# Implementation Plan: JSON Pointer Resolution
+
+**Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md)
+
+## Technical Context
+- Language: TypeScript (strict, ESM, NodeNext), no runtime dependencies.
+- Tests: `node --test` (Node 22, built-in type stripping; relative imports use `.ts` extension).
+- Constitution: unfilled template; no gates. Governing rule from README: follow the published standard (RFC 6901).
+
+## Design
+- `src/pointer.ts`: `parsePointer(pointer): string[]` (validation + unescape) and `resolvePointer`.
+- `src/index.ts`: re-exports `resolvePointer` (and `parsePointer`, reusable by later features).
+- Evaluation: for each token, arrays require `^(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$` and index < length; objects require own property; anything else throws.
+
+## Contract
+`resolvePointer(document: unknown, pointer: string): unknown` — throws `Error` on invalid or unresolvable pointer.
+
+## Validation
+`npm test` runs `test/pointer.test.ts` covering the RFC §5 table and spec edge cases.
